# SelahCue developer AI provider keys — DEVELOPER BUILDS ONLY.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the repository root and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored;
# this sample is not, which is why it must never carry a value, a sample value, or anything that
# looks like one.
#
# The operator reads these only when built with the `dev-keys` Cargo feature, which is off by
# default:
#
#     cargo run --manifest-path implementation/desktop/crates/selahcue-operator/Cargo.toml \
#         --features dev-keys
#
# A default build does not read this file at all — the read is not compiled in. See
# implementation/desktop/crates/selahcue-operator/src/dev_env.rs.
#
# THIS IS TEMPORARY. The shipping path holds no key on a workstation: Deepgram credentials
# become short-lived tokens minted by the SelahCue platform (POST /v1/stt/session), and sermon
# notes stay proxied through the platform API. Both are already ticketed.
#
# Leave a variable blank and it stays UNSET rather than empty, and the operator prints a line
# naming it at startup. Only the three names below are ever read from this file; anything else
# here is parsed and discarded. Two are credentials; the third is a QA convenience and is
# explained where it appears.
#
# Two parsing rules worth knowing:
#   * An inline comment ends a value:  KEY=abc # note   ->  the key is "abc", not "abc # note".
#     Quote the value if a "#" is genuinely part of your key:  KEY="abc # real"
#   * A "#" with no space before it stays:  KEY=abc#def  ->  the key is "abc#def".

# Deepgram streaming transcription (ClickUp 86akby4yz).
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# OpenAI sermon notes (ClickUp 86akby7d8).
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- QA convenience, NOT a credential -------------------------------------------------
# Which OpenAI model generates sermon notes (86akby7d8). Lets physical QA switch tiers
# without a rebuild. Leave BLANK or omit entirely to use the shipped default,
# `gpt-5.6-terra` — a blank value is left unset, so there is one meaning for "unset",
# not two.
#
# This is the only name in the loader's allowlist that is not a credential, and it is
# scaffolding for the developer-key phase: model choice properly belongs in the operator's
# persisted settings (86akbzxyc) and this override dies with the loader.
#
# Known-good values at the time of writing: gpt-5.6-terra (default), gpt-5.6-luna
# (cheaper and faster, but numbers its own outline headings). An unknown model is NOT
# rejected locally — OpenAI's catalogue moves — it comes back as a visible
# "not configured" error naming the rejection, rather than silently falling back.
SELAHCUE_OPENAI_MODEL=
